# Copy to `.env`. All four sources work with NO keys — every variable below is
# optional and only upgrades or hardens an already-working provider.
#
# WARNING: Expo inlines any EXPO_PUBLIC_* value into the JS bundle at build
# time, so anyone who downloads the app can extract it. Fine for local
# development. For production, put these on a backend and point the provider's
# base URL at your proxy — no other code changes.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Congress — no key needed for House trades.
#
# The House Clerk's index says WHO filed a trade report and WHEN; the tickers,
# amounts and directions are inside each filing's PDF. `npm run scrape:house`
# reads those PDFs (about 9 in 10 are electronic; the rest are scanned paper
# and keep a link-to-the-PDF card) and writes
# src/providers/congress/data/house-trades.json, which ships with the app.
# Re-run it to pick up new filings — it only downloads what's new.
#
# Optional: a hosted copy of that file (e.g. the raw GitHub URL the scheduled
# workflow in .github/workflows/scrape-house-trades.yml keeps updated). When
# set, the app prefers it, so new filings appear without a rebuild.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
EXPO_PUBLIC_CONGRESS_TRADES_URL=

# Optional aggregators, for the Senate (which the Clerk path cannot reach).
# Quiver is a paid plan (~$25/mo). FMP's FREE plan does NOT include the
# congressional endpoints — a free key is refused and the app falls back to
# the House data above. Quiver is preferred when both are set.
EXPO_PUBLIC_QUIVER_API_TOKEN=
EXPO_PUBLIC_FMP_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Stocks / price reaction — OPTIONAL.
#
# StocksProvider defaults to Yahoo Finance's public endpoints, which need no
# key. Yahoo is undocumented and rate-limits aggressively; set a Finnhub key to
# use that instead for steadier limits. https://finnhub.io/register
#
# Caution: Finnhub's free plan no longer includes daily candles (`stock/candle`),
# which every price reaction needs. With a free key set, charts and "vs S&P 500"
# go blank. Leave this empty unless the key is on a paid plan.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
EXPO_PUBLIC_FINNHUB_API_KEY=

# Development only. When price lookups fail (e.g. CORS on `expo start --web`),
# fill the Stocks source with a sample series badged SAMPLE DATA. Congress and
# insider reactions never use it. Leave unset for any build you distribute.
EXPO_PUBLIC_DEMO_PRICES=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Insiders (SEC EDGAR) and Policy (Federal Register) need no configuration.
#
# SEC does require a descriptive User-Agent with a real contact address, which
# is hardcoded in src/providers/insider/InsiderProvider.ts — change it to your
# own before shipping. It is how the SEC contacts you instead of silently
# blocking your users.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
